    {
      "id": "fixer",
      "type": "uipath.agent.autonomous",
      "typeVersion": "1.4",
      "display": {
        "label": "Fixer",
        "subLabel": "",
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "icon": "autonomous-agent"
      },
      "inputs": {
        "systemPrompt": "You write small fixes for failing Playwright e2e tests, working on a Windows robot VM through the vm_exec tool. The repository is already cloned at C:\\vm-agent\\repo (git, node, corepack/pnpm and rg on PATH). You are given an investigator notebook that names the cause of the failure.\n\nONLY write a fix when ALL of these hold:\n- the cause lives in test code or page objects under e2e/ (never product source under packages/ or apps/),\n- the notebook explains the mechanism end to end (file:line, what value is wrong and why),\n- the change is small and local (a few lines in one or two files).\nOtherwise set patchWritten=false and in fixSummary say exactly what a human would need to change and why you declined.\n\nWhen you do fix:\n- Batch. Every vm_exec call costs 45-75 s of fixed overhead and is killed after 3 minutes; output is capped at 8000 chars. One call = one complete step, with Write-Output '### <label>' separators and $ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'. Filter with rg -n, Select-String, Select-Object -First N; read only the lines you need, never whole files.\n- Edit files with PowerShell: read -> replace -> write (Get-Content -Raw, .Replace(...), Set-Content -NoNewline), or `git apply` of a patch written from a here-string.\n- Then, in the same script: `git -C C:\\vm-agent\\repo diff > C:\\vm-agent\\notes\\<runId>\\fix.patch`, print the patch (`Get-Content` it) and confirm it is non-empty, then `git -C C:\\vm-agent\\repo checkout -- .` so the working tree is clean again.\n- Do NOT run the test yourself. A later step applies fix.patch and runs it.\n- Never touch remote state (no git push, commit, publish, branch deletion) and never install global packages.\n\nAlways append a `## Fix attempt N` section to C:\\vm-agent\\notes\\<runId>\\NOTES.md (Add-Content; never overwrite) with the rationale: what you changed, why it should fix the mechanism, or why you declined. Do this at the tail of your last vm_exec script, not as a separate call.\n\nOutput fields:\n- patchWritten: true only if fix.patch exists and is non-empty.\n- fixSummary: what you changed and why, or what a human needs to change and why you declined.\n- confidence: high | medium | low.",
        "userPrompt": "Fix attempt {{ $vars.fixAttempts }} of 3.\n\nRun context:\n- repository: {{ $vars.start.output.repoUrl }} @ {{ $vars.start.output.branch }}\n- test command: {{ $vars.start.output.testCommand }}\n- runId: {{ $vars.deriveRunId.output }}  (notebook: C:\\vm-agent\\notes\\{{ $vars.deriveRunId.output }}\\NOTES.md)\n- test exit code: {{ $vars.testEvidence.output.exitCode }}\n- test output tail:\n{{ $vars.testEvidence.output.stdout }}\n\nInvestigator notebook:\n{{ $vars.readNotes.output.Stdout }}\n\nPrevious verification output (empty on the first attempt; otherwise the failed verification of your previous patch):\n{{ $vars.verifyFix.output.Stdout }}\n\nIf the previous verification output is non-empty, read its error lines: your earlier patch did not make the test pass. Write a DIFFERENT patch that addresses what the verification showed, or set patchWritten=false if the notebook's cause does not hold up.\n\nDecide whether the cause qualifies (test code under e2e/, mechanism explained end to end, small local change). If it does, write the fix, produce fix.patch, reset the tree, and append the `## Fix attempt {{ $vars.fixAttempts }}` section to the notebook. If it does not, append the section explaining why you declined and set patchWritten=false. Then return patchWritten, fixSummary and confidence.",
        "model": "anthropic.claude-sonnet-5",
        "mode": "standard",
        "temperature": 0.05,
        "maxTokenPerResponse": 16384,
        "maxIterations": 100,
        "isConversational": false,
        "guardrails": [],
        "name": "fixer",
        "agentInputVariables": [
          {
            "id": "start__output__testCommand",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.start.output.testCommand"
          },
          {
            "id": "start__output__repoUrl",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.start.output.repoUrl"
          },
          {
            "id": "start__output__branch",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.start.output.branch"
          },
          {
            "id": "start__output__runId",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.deriveRunId.output"
          },
          {
            "id": "testEvidence__output__exitCode",
            "type": "integer",
            "binding": "=$vars.testEvidence.output.exitCode"
          },
          {
            "id": "testEvidence__output__stdout",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.testEvidence.output.stdout"
          },
          {
            "id": "readNotes__output__Stdout",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.readNotes.output.Stdout"
          },
          {
            "id": "verifyFix__output__Stdout",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=$vars.verifyFix?.output?.Stdout ?? ''"
          },
          {
            "id": "fixAttempts",
            "type": "number",
            "binding": "=$vars.fixAttempts"
          }
        ],
        "agentOutputVariables": [
          {
            "id": "patchWritten",
            "type": "boolean",
            "required": true,
            "description": "true only if fix.patch was written and is non-empty"
          },
          {
            "id": "fixSummary",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true,
            "description": "What was changed and why, or why no fix was written"
          },
          {
            "id": "confidence",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true,
            "description": "high | medium | low"
          }
        ],
        "source": "86439ed0-f87f-4651-b049-9b2b870842c3",
        "modelMaxTokens": 128000
